{
  "id": "daily-temperatures-with-stack",
  "questionId": "daily-temperatures-with-stack",
  "slug": "daily-temperatures-with-stack",
  "title": "Daily Temperatures",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Stack",
  "patterns": [
    "stack",
    "monotonic stack"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "this is 'days until next greater element' - each day is only waiting on one specific future day, the next one that's warmer. how could you track many pending waiters efficiently?",
    "keep a stack of indices for days whose answer isn't known yet; walk through the temperatures left to right",
    "when the current day's temperature is strictly warmer than the temperature at the index on top of the stack, that's the answer for the popped day: current index minus popped index",
    "keep popping and resolving while the current temperature beats the stack top, then push the current index (its own answer is still unknown)"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using >= instead of strict > when comparing, incorrectly resolving days with equal temperatures",
    "storing temperatures on the stack instead of indices, which makes it impossible to compute the day-distance for the answer",
    "forgetting indices left on the stack at the end never found a warmer day and should keep their default 0"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of daily `temperatures`.\n\n**For each day, find how many days you'd have to wait until a strictly warmer temperature occurs, and return the list of wait counts, one per day.**\n\nIf there's no future day with a warmer temperature, use 0 for that day instead.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= temperatures.length <= 1000",
      "1 <= temperatures[i] <= 100",
      "\"warmer\" means strictly greater than the current day's temperature"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "strictly decreasing temperatures (every day gets 0)",
      "all equal temperatures (every day gets 0, since none is strictly warmer)",
      "a single day (always 0, no future day to compare)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "temperatures = [73, 74, 75, 71, 69, 72, 76, 73]",
        "output": "[1, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0]",
        "explanation": "day 0 (73) waits 1 day for 74; day 2 (75) waits 4 days for 76 at index 6; the last two days never see a warmer day, so 0"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "temperatures = [30, 40, 50, 60]",
        "output": "[1, 1, 1, 0]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 1, 1, 0]",
        "explanation": "strictly increasing temperatures mean each day only waits one day for the next warmer one, except the last"
      },
